             (-)*56(+)*57

             It's now cycle three eight one six nine and we have seven
             max height decoys between here and our flag; additionally
             the tape length is almost certainly at least eighteen if
             the opponent is a /presumably slow/ rush program or else
             the opponent would not have been locked due to rule of
             nine; and the opponent probably isn't a turtle because
             they would have broken the lock by now

             Time to rush!

             We start at the eighteenth cell because any active
             program will have disturbed us earlier if the tape is
             shorter; in case of passive vibration programs we do
             some countervibration

             
             (>+--+.+--+)*8

             We predict no interference from the opponent; so we use
             a two cycle offset clear as our main clear strategy

             If the opponent does interfere it can only be via
             shudder vibration or lock; the opponent cannot take our
             flag before time runs out so we simply ensure that we
             test a cell twice in a row before moving onward; a
             flexible timer clear strategy is used just in case the
             opponent is a passive defender

             (>[(+)*10([-{[+.]}[+--[+--]]
               >[(+)*20([-{[+.]}[+--[+--]]
                >[(+)*22([-{[+.]}[+--[+--]]
                 >[(+)*22([-{[+.]}[+--[+--]]
                  >[(+)*20([-{[+.]}[+--[+--]]
                   >[(+)*20([-{[+.]}[+--[+--]]
                    >[(+)*22([-{[+.]}[+--[+--]]
